<title>UK: Hanson active as rumours of bid persist.</title>
<headline>Hanson active as rumours of bid persist.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hanson Plc, half way through its demerger, were active on Friday amid vague rumours of an impending bid, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares were unchanged at 80-1/2p as some 5.3 million shares changed hands by 1038 GMT making it among the most actively traded shares in London.</p>
<p>Dealers said the rumours crept into the market yesterday, buoying the share price.</p>
<p>&quot;I think you have to give it some credibility because the share price is so cheap,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>The stock fell sharply after the details of its demerger were announced.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
